<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Italia (Social War confederation)</h1><p class="st-meta">91 BCE – 88 BCE · capital Corfinium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rebel state formed by Rome's Italian allies in the Social War of 91–88 BCE, with its own capital, senate, consuls and coinage.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>For two centuries <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome's</a> Italian allies supplied soldiers for its wars without full citizenship. When the tribune <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-livius-drusus-tribune-91-bce">Marcus Livius Drusus</a>, who proposed giving it to them, was murdered in 91 BCE, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marsi">Marsi</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/paeligni">Paeligni</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/samnite-league">Samnites</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/picentes">Picentes</a> and other peoples rose in revolt, starting with a massacre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ascoli-piceno">Asculum</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The rebels set up a federal state modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corfinium">Corfinium</a> as its capital, renamed Italia, a senate of 500 members and two consuls, the Marsian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-poppaedius-silo">Quintus Poppaedius Silo</a> and the Samnite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-papius-mutilus">Gaius Papius Mutilus</a>. They minted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins, some inscribed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a> as Víteliú, showing the Italian bull goring the Roman wolf. Their armies, trained in Roman methods, fought Rome on equal terms in 90 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> divided the rebels by granting citizenship to loyal allies in 90 BCE and to all who laid down arms in 89 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-pompeius-strabo">Pompeius Strabo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Marius</a> defeated the remaining forces, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-poppaedius-silo">Silo</a> was killed in 88 BCE. Within a generation all free Italians south of the Po were Roman citizens.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 91 BCE – 88 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:57.89%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>91 BCE – 88 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Corfinium</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Quintus Poppaedius Silo, Gaius Papius Mutilus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Italic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oscan, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Italia, Italic Confederation</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-90&amp;focus=italia-social-war-confederation" aria-label="Italia (Social War confederation) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5016 679 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Italia (Social War confederation) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5336 935L5353 955M5336 935L5331 938M5336 935L5304 942M5336 935L5361 966"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5353 955h0M5331 938h0M5304 942h0M5361 966h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5336 935h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5336 935h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Corfinium. <a href="/atlas?year=-90&amp;focu